      "id": "eu-generational-renewal-strategy",
      "name": "Strategy for Generational Renewal in Agriculture",
      "kind": "POLICY",
      "status": "ACTIVE",
      "scope": {
        "level": "EU"
      },
      "operator": "European Commission",
      "operatorType": "PUBLIC",
      "whatItOffers": "EU policy framework to make farming more accessible: support for starting, fairer and more transparent land markets, earlier farm succession and pension security, training and rural services. It proposes a Starter Pack for Young Farmers as a single national entry point to funding, training and advice, and aims to double the share of young and new farmers by 2040.",
      "whoCanUseIt": "Member States designing their measures; young farmers and new entrants as the target group.",
      "howToAccess": "Read the Strategy: the Commission's Communication is linked from this page under Documents. Each Member State will prepare its own strategy for generational renewal as part of its National and Regional Partnership Plan.",
      "accessUrl": "https://agriculture.ec.europa.eu/vision-overview/generational-renewal_en",
      "languages": ["en"],
      "targetProfiles": ["YOUNG_FARMER", "NEW_ENTRANT", "SUCCESSOR", "TRANSFEROR"],
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://agriculture.ec.europa.eu/vision-overview/generational-renewal_en",
          "title": "Generational renewal in agriculture",
          "consultedOn": "2026-11-25",
          "quotes": [
            "Read the Strategy",
            "Communication: Strategy for generational renewal in agriculture",
            "Each Member State will prepare a comprehensive strategy for generational renewal as part of its National and Regional Partnership Plan.",
            "The Strategy for Generational Renewal in Agriculture sets out a comprehensive policy framework",
            "Access to land remains one of the biggest barriers for new entrants",
            "Creating a European Land Observatory to improve transparency on land use, ownership and prices",
            "It provides a coordinated EU and national response by combining financial support, fairer land markets, training, and reforms that promote timely farm succession and adequate pension security for retiring farmers.",
            "Investment in rural infrastructure and services such as childcare, healthcare, transport and broadband.",
            "A Starter Pack for Young Farmers will offer a single-entry point at national level, bringing together funding, training and advisory services.",
            "By 2040, Europe aims to double the share of young and new farmers, ensuring that agriculture remains innovative, competitive and resilient."
          ],
          "verification": {
            "checkedOn": "2026-11-25",
            "method": "FETCH"
          }
        }
      ],
      "notes": "The Starter Pack and the European Land Observatory are measures the Strategy announces, not services operating today; the Observatory is documented separately as announced.",
      "generatorId": "claude-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "eu-cap-young-farmers",
      "name": "CAP 2023-27 support for young farmers",
      "kind": "POLICY",
      "status": "ACTIVE",
      "scope": {
        "level": "EU"
      },
      "operator": "European Commission",
      "operatorType": "PUBLIC",
      "whatItOffers": "Explains the CAP 2023-27 support for young farmers that every country tailors in its CAP Strategic Plan: the Complementary Income Support for Young Farmers (CISYF), an annual payment per eligible hectare or lump sum for young farmers newly set up for the first time, plus installation aid, investment support and cooperation for farm succession.",
      "whoCanUseIt": "Young farmers as each country defines them within the EU rules: at most 35 to 40 years old (each country sets the exact limit), head of the holding with effective control over it, and with appropriate training or skills. CISYF is for those newly set up for the first time and entitled to basic income support.",
      "howToAccess": "Apply to the managing authorities listed in your country's CAP Strategic Plan. Most countries pay CISYF under direct payments and open calls for application under rural development funds.",
      "accessUrl": "https://agriculture.ec.europa.eu/common-agricultural-policy/income-support/young-farmers_en",
      "languages": ["en"],
      "targetProfiles": ["YOUNG_FARMER", "NEW_ENTRANT"],
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://agriculture.ec.europa.eu/common-agricultural-policy/income-support/young-farmers_en",
          "title": "Young farmers",
          "consultedOn": "2026-11-17",
          "quotes": [
            "The CAP 2023-27 provides for several interventions specifically for young farmers",
            "EU countries must dedicate an amount corresponding to at least 3% of their direct payments budget to support young farmers",
            "in the context of farm succession, this applies in particular for generational renewal at farm level",
            "The CISYF is a voluntary scheme under direct payments providing enhanced income support to young farmers who are newly set up for the first time and who are entitled to basic income support.",
            "The support is granted in the form of an annual payment per eligible hectare or annual lump sum.",
            "a young farmer can be maximum 35-40 years old (EU countries are to set the exact upper age limit)",
            "must have an effective control over the holding",
            "a young farmer must have appropriate training and/or skills",
            "Young farmers in the EU can apply for CAP support to the managing authorities, which are listed in their country’s national CAP Strategic Plan.",
            "Most EU countries support generational renewal through CISYF under direct payments and via rural development funds call for application."
          ],
          "verification": {
            "checkedOn": "2026-11-24",
            "method": "FETCH"
          }
        }
      ],
      "generatorId": "claude-2"
